From 71b245f4075ad705e5b62667821b798317550066 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt C <latentcollapse@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:28:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 24/42] nira: make the NeuraJL operator usable for scored D
 trials

scripts/abc-agent.ts is B's trial runner with only the tool surface
changed: one `neurajl` tool, the same 60s tool limit, request budget,
retry, compaction and headless-completion handling as B and C.

The adapter:
- binds the agent's cwd as the kernel's writable working directory; the
  kernel previously could not see the task at all
- returns captured printed output with a REPL-style value display
- throws on failure; the agent loop ignores an `isError` field on a
  returned result, so errors were reported to the model as successes
- stops the kernel on abort, and when a kernel has died the next call
  starts a new one and states that all earlier bindings are gone
- takes the bridge's explicit session_dead flag instead of racing its
  exit, and treats "close" rather than "exit" as the end of output
- stops the bridge with stdin EOF, then SIGTERM, before SIGKILL, so its
  sandbox and depot clone are torn down
- optional middle-elided cap on model-visible output

The substrate tests never type-checked (4-argument AgentTool.execute
called with 5; `isError` read off AgentToolResult) and bound the repo
checkout writable as the workspace. Rewritten against a temp workspace
to cover persistence, printed output, host-visible writes, errors,
ephemeral isolation, timeout recovery and dispose.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
